A template result whose type does not depend on the type parameter (int) is
produced identically by every instantiation, so instantiating the template at two
types (T=int and T=string, via the two consumers) produces int twice. plumb
rejects it as ambiguous, naming the real cause (the type-parameter-independent
result) rather than reporting the provider as colliding with itself.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
error-is: ErrAmbiguousProducer
-- example.com/app/a.go --
package app

type Box[T any] struct{ V T }

//plumb:build
func Make[T any]() (Box[T], int) { var b Box[T]; return b, 0 }

//plumb:build
func UseInt(b Box[int]) string { return "" }

//plumb:build
func UseString(b Box[string]) bool { return false }
